<title>GERMANY: Colonia 1996 non-life profits rise.</title>
<headline>Colonia 1996 non-life profits rise.</headline>
<dateline>COLOGNE, Germany 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit Nordstern Allgemeine	104.9   vs 82.5</p>
<p>    Net profit Colonia Versicherung	 78     vs 72.9</p>
<p>    Premium income (non-life)		5,830   up 5.3 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German insurer is CKAG Colonia Konzern AG. The results refer to its two main non-life insurance units.  </p>
<p>    Dividend Nordstern common shares     30 pct vs 26 pct</p>
<p>		 Nordstern pref shares	 32 pct vs 28 pct</p>
<p>    Dividend Colonia			    32 pct vs 28 pct</p>
<p>		 plus bonus			 20 pct vs n/a</p>
<p>NOTE - The premium income figure refers to Colonia's total global non-life business. The company said in a statement that premium income at Colonia Versicherung and Nordstern Allgemeine, the domestic units, had fallen slightly. Colonia is part of the newly formed giant French insurance group Axa. Outside shareholders in Nordstern will also receive a guaranteed dividend of 113.5 percent per common share and 115.5 percent per preferred share, the company said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
